{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it","id":1089244,"title":"Why do you think, that Dragon's Ire is bad and how would you fix it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T10:29:37-07:00","id":1089244,"title":"Why do you think, that Dragon's Ire is bad and how would you fix it?","content":"That...........","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:36:34-07:00","id":1089247,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how I would fix it off hand, but.. okay. Dragon's Ire, as I've otherwise put it: It's a nice idea to turn it into an actual full out art, it really is. But this is basically an art where you want to use it if you end up in a fight, it's noted as the big fighty combat art of combat. But whereas it used to be a reflexive action to invoke the Ire for a scene, now not. So you're already taking a round to cast whatever personal buff power of the ones available, you're further splitting that casting action if you want to bunk at all, and the duration is limited to rounds barring use of time. That feels basically useless and kinda pointless. If the idea is &quot;really only useful with time to prepare&quot;, the short durations don't help that either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:41:48-07:00","id":1089257,"title":"","content":"I suppose I'd fiddle around with extending the durations or maybe some kind of &quot;spend an extra point of willpower, cast the personal buff powers reflexively&quot; or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:14:10-07:00","id":1089371,"title":"","content":"Time 3. Trigger: My sword leaves its scabbard.<br /> <br /> Just don't overdo it or you can expect your gm to have fun with other things causing your sword to leave its scabbard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T21:00:38-07:00","id":1089565,"title":"","content":"I'd really kick up the duration to &quot;one conflict&quot; that's my fix. Once its out of combat rounds power ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T22:59:04-07:00","id":1089597,"title":"","content":"Speaking of duration, can you apply multiple levels of Time to the same cantrip with no extra effect after the first one?<br /> <br /> For example, Time 1, 3 and 4 can make, say, Dragon's Ire 2 apply for 2 turns +3 per success starting the next time someone tries to attack you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T02:49:36-07:00","id":1090193,"title":"","content":"There was bunk called &quot;participating a duel with deadly weapons&quot;. Certain bunks can be much quicker, than others depending on their circumstances and player's creativity. Just imagine, that deadly combat isn't a default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T03:01:00-07:00","id":1090201,"title":"","content":"It would make sense if the attack roll counted as the bunk for Dragon's Ire. Thus, it'd be a reflexive effect. Having to skip your first round of combat to activate the powers would be a distinct disadvantage in WoD combat, where attack-first is everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:56:02-07:00","id":1090235,"title":"","content":"I can't say I'm adept at World of Darkness combat, as most of scuffles I've witnessed were either a situation comedy or super-deadly towards opposition anyway.<br /> <br /> Well, being hit also can be considered a good bunk. For defensive and punitive Cantrips alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-09-2017, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:57:19-07:00","id":1090277,"title":"","content":"Of course, there might be a social etiquette thing, where changelings give each other a turn to draw swords, or take ten paces, or activate their Dragon's Ire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe"