alue":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:46:59-07:00","id":1090464,"title":"","content":"They'll also politely wait until you done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T14:39:10-07:00","id":1090486,"title":"","content":"You know what they say. If you find yourself in a fair fight, you're a disgrace to House Eiluned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T15:35:57-07:00","id":1090502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1090486#post1090486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what they say. If you find yourself in a fair fight, you're a disgrace to House Eiluned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Bunks are about making reality go &quot;what are you doing?&quot; You should especially get your oponent to pause and ask said question, observe this helpful demonstration<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jaaJyAjvajo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jaaJyAjvajo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jaaJyAjvajo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jaaJyAjvajo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T16:46:34-07:00","id":1090518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1090486#post1090486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what they say. If you find yourself in a fair fight, you're a disgrace to House Eiluned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Metamorphosis 5 is your solution for most duels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-09-2017, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T09:53:41-07:00","id":1090758,"title":"","content":"I don't necessarily think that The Dragon's Ire is <i>bad</i> but if I were to design it I would keep it formatted around the idea that invoking the Ire is like turning on a mode, like Sailor Moon upgrading to Super Sailor Moon, or going Super Saiyan. With that in mind, I would make the first dot of the Art Tripping the Ire, basically &quot;turning the mode on.&quot; Every dot after that would give you access to different benefits while Tripping the Ire, such as the damage bonus, to-hit bonus, soak bonus, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:11:30-07:00","id":1090766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gl1tterboots</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1090758#post1090758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't necessarily think that The Dragon's Ire is <i>bad</i> but if I were to design it I would keep it formatted around the idea that invoking the Ire is like turning on a mode, like Sailor Moon upgrading to Super Sailor Moon, or going Super Saiyan. With that in mind, I would make the first dot of the Art Tripping the Ire, basically &quot;turning the mode on.&quot; Every dot after that would give you access to different benefits while Tripping the Ire, such as the damage bonus, to-hit bonus, soak bonus, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like a Contract Art you mean?<br /> <br /> Interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:17:40-07:00","id":1090771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1090766#post1090766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much like a Contract Art you mean?<br /> <br /> Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it preserves the idea that the Ire was a changeling's &quot;combat mode&quot; in previous editions, as opposed to a collection of spells. This way, the Dragon's Ire is something you hone as you progress through the Art, unlocking different features that can be used while you're Tripping the Ire.<br /> <br /> ETA: Plus, it fixes the whole &quot;bunks in mid-combat to cast new Ire Cantrips to modify my attacks&quot; bit which can disrupt the momentum of combat scenes, both from an in-character perspective and an out-of-character perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:40:55-07:00","id":1090781,"title":"","content":"Would you eliminate Glamour costs for each of the additional abilities?<br /> <br /> Like someone buys Dragon's Ire 5 with freebies, casts it once and goes all-out Hulk on enemies? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:58:06-07:00","id":1090791,"title":"","content":"No, I don't think so. Invoking each benefit would require Glamour (unless Chimerical, per the rules). I think, with the respect that the developers want to keep Arts from being &quot;landlocked&quot; by Realm, you can still use cantrips of Dragon's Ire on other things. I'd probably use language that the main benefit of Tripping the Ire is that you can use the rest of the Art on yourself reflexively each turn (ala Celerity) as opposed to needing a new Bunk + Art/Realm roll as you would to affect someone/something not Tripping the Ire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T11:04:33-07:00","id":1090793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gl1tterboots</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1090791#post1090791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't think so. Invoking each benefit would require Glamour (unless Chimerical, per the rules). I think, with the respect that the developers want to keep Arts from being &amp;quot;landlocked&amp;quot; by Realm, you can still use cantrips of Dragon's Ire on other things. I'd probably use language that the main benefit of Tripping the Ire is that you can use the rest of the Art on yourself reflexively each turn (ala Celerity) as opposed to needing a new Bunk + Art/Realm roll as you would to affect someone/something not Tripping the Ire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea.<br /> <br /> Really, Dragon's Ire, as it was, should just remain a subsystem (but make it dependent on your Glamour rating, not Remembrance). Perhaps require that the changeling Invoke the Wyrd to activate it, so that it's a specific battle form/horrid form.<br /> <br /> Then the new Dragon's Ire Art should be the revised Discord Art, which modifies that base combat ability of the fae in the same way that Contracts modifies the base system for oaths. Plus, calling it Discord also allows us to retain the naming convention of the other Arts (one word only).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-10-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T11:27:38-07:00","id":1090801,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, you could make it a bit like Shadow Dice. You can invoke the Dragon's Ire by rolling Glamour, but each success gives you an extra point of Nightmare as you call on the horrors of the Dreaming. But that might put too negative a spin on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T11:34:32-07:00","id":1090803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1090793#post1090793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good idea.<br /> <br /> Really, Dragon's Ire, as it was, should just remain a subsystem (but make it dependent on your Glamour rating, not Remembrance). Perhaps require that the changeling Invoke the Wyrd to activate it, so that it's a specific battle form/horrid form.<br /> <br /> Then the new Dragon's Ire Art should be the revised Discord Art, which modifies that base combat ability of the fae in the same way that Contracts modifies the base system for oaths. Plus, calling it Discord also allows us to retain the naming convention of the other Arts (one word only).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't mind keeping Dragon's Ire as a subsystem (similar to Embracing the Wyrd in Lost 2E), and I think Nightmare Dice would be an apropos tradeoff for invoking that dangerous faerie power. To that extent, I agree that a revised Discord would work nicely in the Art's current place in the roster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T11:57:24-07:00","id":1090809,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to ask that at this point is it likely that it will change, if the consensus says it doesn't work as intended?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T12:49:23-07:00","id":1090825,"title":"","content":"I dunno. There's isn't many people who are against it and we haven't heard anybody defending Dragon's Ire in its current state.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it a consensus, per se.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:32:16-07:00","id":1090844,"title":"","content":"It seems unlikely, they're just collecting errata now. I'm pretty sure that otherwise what we see is what we get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:58:19-07:00","id":1090884,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they've already done layout. I could see maybe power level tweaks, but not a full rewrite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:27:25-07:00","id":1090894,"title":"","content":"Which is a shame when the arts are overall such good stuff as far as being the otherwise sour note there, but yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:47:40-07:00","id":1090897,"title":"","content":"I still think just making all the durations last a scene gets you most of the way there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:12:39-07:00","id":1090907,"title":"","content":"I'm certainly going to give that a shot when I run, yeah, maybe along with the &quot;increased costs to cast reflexively&quot; or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:43:06-07:00","id":1090919,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that fights don't generally start a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T01:18:52-07:00","id":1091013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1090793#post1090793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good idea.<br /> <br /> Really, Dragon's Ire, as it was, should just remain a subsystem (but make it dependent on your Glamour rating, not Remembrance). Perhaps require that the changeling Invoke the Wyrd to activate it, so that it's a specific battle form/horrid form.<br /> <br /> Then the new Dragon's Ire Art should be the revised Discord Art, which modifies that base combat ability of the fae in the same way that Contracts modifies the base system for oaths. Plus, calling it Discord also allows us to retain the naming convention of the other Arts (one word only).</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as the person who not only wrote the new Dragon's Ire, but was primary champion for making it an Art rather than innate power:<br /> <br /> With respect, I think you are <i>greatly</i> underestimating how powerful Dragon's Ire was back in 2e. It was an effect I would give a great deal to get ahold of in Exalted, never mind Changeling.<br /> <br /> The new Art is pretty formidable if you either have prep time, are willing to skip bunks, or use Time to extend its duration or trigger-prep it in advance. Or if, God help your enemies, you combine it with Scene to buff your entire motley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":84,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","user":"Holden","date":". 05-11-2017, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T01:29:22-07:00","id":1091016,"title":"","content":"For my part, I must say that I feel really grateful that the Dragon's Ire has become an Art, because having to remind constantly my players of special powers/weakness who aren't printed on their sheet is fatiguing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T02:08:26-07:00","id":1091022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1091013#post1091013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking as the person who not only wrote the new Dragon's Ire, but was primary champion for making it an Art rather than innate power:<br /> <br /> With respect, I think you are <i>greatly</i> underestimating how powerful Dragon's Ire was back in 2e. It was an effect I would give a great deal to get ahold of in Exalted, never mind Changeling.<br /> <br /> The new Art is pretty formidable if you either have prep time, are willing to skip bunks, or use Time to extend its duration or trigger-prep it in advance. Or if, God help your enemies, you combine it with Scene to buff your entire motley.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. At least, not in my experience. You were allowed up to your Remembrance in successes (no more than five, therefore) and these added extra dice to a physical dice pool, not successes (three extra dice usually results in an average of one extra success). You're going to end up with one or two extra successes at most--usually one or fewer.<br /> <br /> It's no more effective than, say, a vampire's blood buffing, a werewolf's Crinos form, a wraith's Shadow Dice. As it is, fae have no innate way of buffing stats for combat and can't just spend Glamour to heal wounds. Even reading over all their powers, at best they can only inflict lethal damage too.<br /> <br /> If you want to play urban fantasy with strong mythic elements and lots of heroism, giving characters some way to actually do that and survive physical encounters is quite valuable. It's not for every table, but it makes for more cinematic encounters.<br /> <br /> Plus, Glamour is still a finite resource. You can't have more points than your permanent rating, so most characters won't be able to do much before they're depleted again. Dragon's Ire as an Art will swallow up even more of that precious Glamour, but for a much reduced benefit in most cases.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I want to crib the Shadow Dice system from Wraith, but using Nightmare Dice instead. Horrors and pain swirl around you if you draw on your inner darkness in this way. It also makes the game feel a little bit more like it fits in the World of Darkness too.<br /> <br /> I know this isn't for everyone, but for games of chivalry and danger, it might make the difference between quick-and-lethal combat and epic-but-glorious battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T03:06:39-07:00","id":1091039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1091013#post1091013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking as the person who not only wrote the new Dragon's Ire, but was primary champion for making it an Art rather than innate power:<br /> <br /> With respect, I think you are <i>greatly</i> underestimating how powerful Dragon's Ire was back in 2e. It was an effect I would give a great deal to get ahold of in Exalted, never mind Changeling.<br /> <br /> The new Art is pretty formidable if you either have prep time, are willing to skip bunks, or use Time to extend its duration or trigger-prep it in advance. Or if, God help your enemies, you combine it with Scene to buff your entire motley.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with the Dragon's Ire Art as it stands now is it's less useful in combat than the other Arts as they stand now, which is a big problem given all Dragon's Ire is good for is combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:07:50-07:00","id":1091052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1091039#post1091039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with the Dragon's Ire Art as it stands now is it's less useful in combat than the other Arts as they stand now, which is a big problem given all Dragon's Ire is good for is combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, too. At level one you can add extra dice to Dexterity or Strength, but it doesn't really get much better. You can tweak a few difficulties or spread the dice between multiple attributes, but that's it. Oh, except for Holly Strike, which now only does lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Okay, here's another approach. How about we move Tripping the Ire to level one, and then each successive level adds additional bonuses. So level two increases the difficulty to hit you by +2. Level three lets you make special claw, teeth and horn attacks that cause aggravated damage. Level four lets you launch a volley of magic like Holly Strike (but still aggravated). Level five lets you become a whirlwind of destruction: your initiative increases by an equal amount to your Tripping the Ire score, and you can heal one level of normal damage per turn at the cost of gaining one point of Nightmare for each level healed.<br /> <br /> Given that some Arts involve resurrection at level five, I don't think this is overpowered, but it's a significant buff to Dragon's Ire as it is.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Anyone else want to take a stab at it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:37:56-07:00","id":1091081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1091013#post1091013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking as the person who not only wrote the new Dragon's Ire, but was primary champion for making it an Art rather than innate power:<br /> <br /> With respect, I think you are <i>greatly</i> underestimating how powerful Dragon's Ire was back in 2e. It was an effect I would give a great deal to get ahold of in Exalted, never mind Changeling.<br /> <br /> The new Art is pretty formidable if you either have prep time, are willing to skip bunks, or use Time to extend its duration or trigger-prep it in advance. Or if, God help your enemies, you combine it with Scene to buff your entire motley.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having to take a turn to combat buff yourself in a fight (and that's if you only want to use one of the personal buffs from it), is pretty lethal in a fight. Even if you skip bunks, it still takes an action to cast, and the action splitting rules aren't that forgiving besides, if you wanted to do something like cast and defend yourself. It takes an ability that could help you out if a fight sprung up and basically only makes it kind of useful with prep time, or if you also buy a bunch of time to go with it as far as setting it up with triggers and otherwise dealing with the duration issues ontop of that.<br /> <br /> edit: And besides anything else, using time with it further adds to the difficulty number for the roll, making for less successes, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-11-2017, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:29:40-07:00","id":1091118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1091013#post1091013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking as the person who not only wrote the new Dragon's Ire, but was primary champion for making it an Art rather than innate power:<br /> <br /> With respect, I think you are <i>greatly</i> underestimating how powerful Dragon's Ire was back in 2e. It was an effect I would give a great deal to get ahold of in Exalted, never mind Changeling.<br /> <br /> The new Art is pretty formidable if you either have prep time, are willing to skip bunks, or use Time to extend its duration or trigger-prep it in advance. Or if, God help your enemies, you combine it with Scene to buff your entire motley.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do want to reiterate that I don't think the new Art is <i>bad</i>. I was just offering an alternate design example. I do think that Dragon's Ire was not overpowered in previous editions, particularly when stacked next to a Garou's healing and form buffs or a vampire's healing and blood buffs. But aside from bemoaning the loss of Dragon's Ire as a subsystem, it seems like the biggest critique at play is that people wanted a combat-focused Art to flow well <i>in combat</i>. Sure, if someone is playing the equivalent of a D&amp;D Bard, using Dragon's Ire as written is great when you're buffing and debuffing instead of attacking. That is very cool and thematic. But that's an outlier situation, I think, and people are wanting it to be more accessible in circumstances like duels where it's not really thematic (halts the momentum is what I said earlier) to alternate turns between casting Cantrips and attacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:05:57-07:00","id":1093369,"title":"","content":"Like many Arts, there are features here that are better cast BEFORE trouble. I love this as an Art, though, and it really puts the fae up there as warriors, something they sort of lacked for a good while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:50:10-07:00","id":1093385,"title":"","content":"I didn't write the Dragon's Ire Art, but I worked on the Art designs. Out of curiosity (and in no way meant as snark), has anyone played with C20 Dragon's Ire RAW? I'm interested to hear how the folks who feel underwhelmed by the new DI Art used it in actual play. I love to hear play feedback from people passionate about a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13387-jonsan","name":"jonsan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:02:10-07:00","id":1093390,"title":"","content":"I'm still in the process of organizing a game. <br /> <br /> Do you know how the closed playtests went for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:13:57-07:00","id":1093395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1093390#post1093390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still in the process of organizing a game.<br /> <br /> Do you know how the closed playtests went for it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't. We had a few playtest groups, but due to the time frame for development and the sheer amount of stuff in this book, we didn't have enough groups and time to test everything in an ongoing chronicle. We did some white room style testing for the Arts, but I don't think I was present for any that used the new DI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13387-jonsan","name":"jonsan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:40:22-07:00","id":1093405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jonsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1093385#post1093385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't write the Dragon's Ire Art, but I worked on the Art designs. Out of curiosity (and in no way meant as snark), has anyone played with C20 Dragon's Ire RAW? I'm interested to hear how the folks who feel underwhelmed by the new DI Art used it in actual play. I love to hear play feedback from people passionate about a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, last weekend we ran a series of one-shot scenes to test out a few rules and see how they support the narrative, because the rules are there to support the story flow. Disclaimer: These were obviously white room scenarios but we gave them emotional stakes and tried to play the truth of them instead of playing them as white room scenarios and rolling dice without any kind of accompanying narration or conflict. We tested Unleashing, the new Time Realm, Dragon's Ire, Mists-that-affect-changelings-in-the-Dreaming, and some of the Epiphany rules. <br /> <br /> We felt that Dragon's Ire does not feel like Dragon's Ire from 2nd Ed (with the exception of Tripping the Ire). Previous devs have posted about the importance of nostalgia in this edition, so I think the comment warrants being said (whether that is a critique or an improvement is completely subjective). Specific to the Cantrips, 1 has a good design. 2 and 3 felt a little too close together, and players weren't sure which one would be more effective to use in the heat of battle. Holly Strike is wholly different from the design of 1-3 but feels the most satisfying to use in battle. It contributed the most to the narrative of the scene and felt the most <i>magical</i> to use (specifically saying that the Cantrip can manifest in multiple thematic forms was very inspiring to players, who interpreted the Cantrip's appearance very differently and personally). We were a little concerned about the change from aggravated to lethal, but using Willpower + Glamour + Successes to calculate damage offset that feeling (rolling more dice = feels cool). Tripping the Ire felt simple and effective, and the idea that it slowly &quot;burns out&quot; is an interesting mechanic that can be specifically called upon in the narration. However, I had a player roll 1 success on activation which meant that the 5 dot power gave her one bonus die that burned out in one turn. That was a bummer. I would consider House Ruling a minimum bonus or duration, like a bonus = to Glamour that depletes after (successes) turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:45:30-07:00","id":1093407,"title":"","content":"How did the durations feel for the first three levels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T14:00:07-07:00","id":1093410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1093407#post1093407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did the durations feel for the first three levels?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Burning Thew felt appropriately brief and powerful for a first-dot power. Players asked me if they allocated all successes to efficacy, do they need to split their dice pool for multiple actions to attack or will they lose the power. I ruled that it would last a single full round, thereby ending at the end of their next turn, because I felt otherwise it wouldn't be cool. However, I could see more hardliner ST's saying that you would have to attack that same turn or lose the benefit. I would consider allowing this Cantrip to be reflexive, because otherwise it bogs down the momentum of combat (unless you're hanging the Cantrip with Time, but I think that the battle Art should still flow well <i>in battle</i> and not just when used before battle).<br /> <br /> <b>ETA: </b>By reflexive, what I mean is I would consider &quot;making an attack&quot; to be one possible appropriate Bunk for Burning Thew, thereby allowing them to cast the Cantrip as they attack instead of dedicating a turn to a bunk that otherwise augments their ability to attack.<br /> <br /> Confounding Coils and Dragonscales have an appropriate duration.<br /> <br /> I will say that the trend I saw was that players spent Willpower on Dragon's Ire more often than other actions, which tells me they were invested in success on these activation rolls the most (assuming because allocating the successes from these cantrips affects how the rest of the combat plays out re: cantrip duration).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","user":"gl1tterboots","date":". 05-16-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}